WEBVTT

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:24.100
Hello, Mr. Kishibe!

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:26.770
It's such a nice day!

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.310
MINORU KAIGAMORI, AGE 23, EDITOR

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.110
What are you reading?

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.320
De Staël.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.700
Dostarl?

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:35.950
Is it a new band or something?

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:42.790
He was a Russian artist. He died in 1955.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.000
Listen, Kaigamori.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.460
ROHAN KISHIBE, AGE 27, MANGA ARTIST

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:49.340
Of course,
it's absolutely unacceptable

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.300
for a professional to be late
for a business appointment, but…

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.340
it's also not right for an editor
to arrive six minutes early

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.680
for an appointment with a manga artist!

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:04.310
I'm sorry. So coming early is wrong too.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:06.600
You were lucky it was me this time.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:11.110
Now, let's talk about my next 61-page
one-shot manga, shall we?

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:14.070
Excuse me, Mr. Kishibe! We are your fans!

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:17.740
Could we have your autograph?
Please write "To Akira"!

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.450
No, no! No autographs, you two!

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.660
Mr. Kishibe is busy! He's working!

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.040
I've signed them already.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:30.090
Unlike some, I'm a fast worker.

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:33.250
I always give my autograph
to thank my fans.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:37.550
Wow! How did you do that?!
Drip painting using coffee!

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:39.840
Thanks, buddy. You rock!

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.430
Gotcha, gotcha, gotcha!

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:44.970
-By the way…
-Huh?

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:48.270
Before we start discussing work,
I need to ask you about something.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:49.440
Sure.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:54.230
To be honest, it's about money.
About my payment. Okay?

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:58.570
Could you pay me in advance?
I've recently gone bankrupt.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:03.740
I'm not in debt yet, but I have no home.

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:04.660
What?!

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:08.870
I'm staying with Koichi for now.
I don't even have a desk to work on.

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:13.000
My <i>Sailor Moon</i> figures,
Led Zeppelin paper-jacket records

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:15.380
and <i>Rurouni Kenshin</i> manga…
I've sold the lot.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:16.920
What did you say?

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:19.590
You don't have an office?
What do you mean, bankrupt?

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.140
Haven't you just bought some mountains?
In a resort village?

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:27.850
Yeah, so that I can do some research
for my comics about a specter

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.440
which supposedly lives there.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.690
Some developer was trying to build
a damn road to the resort village.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:36.900
So, I bought six mountains around there
to stop the construction.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:40.660
See, I needed to buy
as much land as possible

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.570
to stop the construction.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:46.830
Then, the resort road plan was scrapped,
so the land price slumped.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:49.660
That place is now just wilderness
in the middle of nowhere.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:53.080
The mountains I bought are worth nothing…

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.550
which means, I'm penniless.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:57.670
Can I get paid in advance?

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.590
Hang on a minute.

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:03.970
Did you buy those hills
to research your manga?

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.890
-Yep.
-Not for an investment?

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.470
No. What I need is reality in my manga.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:11.100
For your research on some specter legend?

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.400
Enough!

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.310
If the road was built,

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.440
that specter might be scared off!

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.400
Then my plan will be wrecked!

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:27.080
Hey, hey! Don't give me that look!
Did you just look away?

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.620
Why are you looking away?

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:31.830
You think I'm off my head, don't you?

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:33.630
Mr. Editor!

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:38.710
Look, a manga artist doesn't always
have to spend his money on super cars

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.380
and gaming rooms in the basement.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:47.560
Besides, it was there.
The research was well worth it.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:53.060
Remember, this story is exclusive
to your magazine.

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:56.190
"It was there"?

00:03:57.190 --> 00:03:59.070
What do you mean "it"?

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:02.320
Haven't you been listening to me?

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:03.780
I saw it with my own eyes.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.990
The specter of Mutsu-kabe Hill
is still there.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:10.450
It's still there now.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:13.920
I'm sorry, Mr. Kishibe, but…

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:19.420
could you please say that again?
What is there?

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:27.390
<i>There was a girl called Naoko Osato,</i>
<i>a university student in her last year.</i>

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:31.600
<i>At the end of September,</i>
<i>she killed her boyfriend.</i>

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:20.110
EPISODE 2: MUTSU-KABE HILL

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:25.950
<i>Naoko Osato…</i>

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:30.410
<i>She is the only daughter of a successful</i>
<i>family in Mutsu-kabe village,</i>

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:33.410
<i>who have been making miso paste</i>
<i>for 300 years.</i>

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:40.630
<i>Their property stood at the end</i>
<i>of a single-lane road on a mountain.</i>

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:44.380
<i>In other words,</i>
<i>they owned the entire mountain.</i>

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:53.930
Gunpei…

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.810
can you go home now ?

00:05:58.230 --> 00:05:59.770
Put away the video game too.

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:03.320
Why?

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:06.190
Has someone come to the main house?

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:09.700
Doesn't matter! Will you just leave now?
From the back door.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:11.200
Nao? Ah…

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:16.080
Nowadays you're, like, a bit cold, huh?

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:20.040
Surely you're not with another guy?

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:25.090
If you've already worked it out,
that makes things easy.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:29.300
At least we've got something nice
to remember.

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:33.890
My father will never let us marry.
You're just a part-time gardener.

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:38.140
As the only daughter,
I'll be responsible for the family estate.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.980
I don't think so!

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:47.240
You're kidding, right?
Why can't we just carry on, Nao?

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:48.190
Let me go.

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:49.860
We don't need to split up.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:51.110
Let go of me!

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:56.990
Shall I show me holding you like this
to your new man and your precious daddy?

00:06:57.580 --> 00:06:59.460
I said let go!

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:02.420
You…

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.250
I-- I'm sorry.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:09.380
B-but you hit me first.

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:13.050
I really love you, Nao.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:15.850
It's fine this way. Nobody needs to know.

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:17.720
Go! Go home!

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:19.480
Nao, listen--

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:22.810
Go! Take that money and go home!

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:29.860
She may get flustered to see you
drop in unannounced.

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:33.280
She'll be desperately trying
to do herself up!

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:38.040
They're coming. I'm stuck!

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:41.120
Please, take your stuff and go now!

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:43.210
I'll be honest with you.

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:44.670
You're awesome.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:47.170
But he's my fiancé.

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:50.760
I'm going to marry him next spring,
after I graduate.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:54.300
So this is the end for us.
We can't see each other any more!

00:07:58.850 --> 00:07:59.680
What?

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:05.230
Gunpei.

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:12.240
Hey.

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:22.750
No.

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:25.420
You're messing with me again…

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:27.250
aren't you?

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:29.090
Gunpei…

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:31.630
stop playing around.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:35.470
No pulse.

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:38.350
He's d-dead.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:44.890
<i>Naoko thought she should</i>
<i>attend</i> <i>to Gunpei's wound anyway.</i>

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:50.230
<i>She pressed a towel she found nearby</i>
<i>onto the wound.</i>

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:55.110
<i>He's playing tricks on me.</i>
<i>This can't be true.</i>

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.030
<i>I just shoved him lightly.</i>

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:02.950
Why was that golf club there?

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:04.620
Why?

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:07.210
It looks as if…

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:11.840
as if I hit him with the golf club!

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:13.300
Gunpei!

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:15.420
What shall I do?

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:18.510
A doctor! I've got to call a doctor!

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:23.520
If he is dead, will a doctor be any good?

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:27.940
Or should I call the police?

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:32.780
Naoko, are you there? It's your father.

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:38.530
Shuichi has come to see you.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:46.710
<i>No, I'm not here.</i>

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:50.130
<i>I don't exist anywhere.</i>

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:53.920
It's locked.

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:57.220
Maybe Naoko is not here…

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:01.550
I may be mistaken, Mr. Osato,

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:04.680
but I think I just saw movement
through the window.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:12.570
I must hide him!

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:15.400
S-somewhere!

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:21.160
<i>I must hide Gunpei!</i>

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:23.990
Under the sofa for now!

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:32.460
What's going on?
He's got no pulse,
and his heart's not beating.

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:34.000
Why's he still bleeding?

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:37.010
Naoko! Are you there?

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:41.050
Are you all right? Is anything wrong?

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:44.140
I've got a spare key. Let me open it…

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:45.140
Father!

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:47.520
I--I didn't hear you!

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:49.480
I was tidying up in the kitchen!

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:52.560
Oh, you are there.

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:54.860
Shuichi is here.

00:10:56.110 --> 00:10:58.070
Oh, I'm so glad!

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:00.490
Please have him wait in the main house!

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:03.570
Your voice sounds a bit odd.

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:05.990
Are you okay? Do you need help?

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:08.000
I'm fine! I'm getting dressed.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:11.710
Please, don't open the door.
I'll be with you in a minute.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:12.790
Please!

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:17.300
Please don't open the door!

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:18.460
FIRST AID

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:22.840
DISINFECTANT

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:36.320
No.

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:46.160
Wh-- what is this?

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:49.620
Can humans bleed after they are dead?

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:52.080
Naoko!

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:56.750
You're using an awful lot of water.
What are you up to?

00:11:57.630 --> 00:12:01.970
It's me, Shuichi.
Are you wondering why I'm still here?

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:08.890
Actually, your father lent me
the spare key so that we can be alone.

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:13.980
No! Don't come in! You mustn't!

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:16.560
Naoko.

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:22.450
Actually, I saw someone
behind the window a while ago.

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:26.160
You don't have anyone in there with you,
do you?

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:29.160
Aren't you alone?

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:33.660
It looked as though
someone else was there with you.

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:40.670
<i>I'm sorry. So sorry!</i>
<i>But this is your fault!</i>

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:42.590
<i>Not mine!</i>

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:58.310
What…

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:02.740
What's going on, Naoko?

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:06.820
So there is someone, then.

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:10.490
Gunpei, please!

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:13.250
Stop it! Please stop it!

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:18.540
I'm opening the door and coming in!

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:51.530
You said you saw someone else here.

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:54.790
So who was it, Shuichi?

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:03.210
<i>Please,</i> <i>please stop.</i>

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:04.170
<i>Stop.</i>

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:07.300
<i>Gunpei, forgive me.</i>

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:10.220
<i>Stop.</i>

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:12.430
<i>Forgive me.</i>

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:17.770
I'm sorry. I was wrong.

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:20.480
I was really mistaken.

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:23.400
I'll be in the main house
with your father.

00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:37.040
<i>So, as arranged, Naoko Osato</i>
<i>married Shuichi the next spring,</i>

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:39.750
<i>and he was welcomed</i>
<i>into the Osato family.</i>

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:44.420
<i>And ever since then…</i>

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:47.920
<i>Gunpei Kamafusa</i>
<i>has never stopped bleeding.</i>

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:52.640
<i>Every day, he quietly bleeds</i>
<i>about 300cc of blood.</i>

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:56.600
<i>If his body is not moved,</i>
<i>he never bleeds more than that.</i>

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:00.020
<i>However,</i>
<i>the bleeding is steady and continuous…</i>

00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:05.360
<i>even though all signs of life</i>
<i>have completely disappeared.</i>

00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:12.700
<i>Naoko Osato has never been on a trip</i>
<i>away from home since her marriage.</i>

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:14.490
<i>Every morning…</i>

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:19.120
<i>Naoko takes a glass jar full</i>
<i>of Gunpei's blood</i>

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:22.460
<i>and discards it secretly.</i>

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:28.130
<i>Every single day, to make sure</i>
<i>that the family won't see it.</i>

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:31.840
Naoko, come and eat with us!

00:15:32.380 --> 00:15:33.760
I'm coming!

00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:45.560
<i>Ever since the detached guest house</i>
<i>was demolished for conversion,</i>

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:51.360
<i>there in the attic above the closet</i>
<i>in the main house lies Gunpei.</i>

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:57.080
<i>One day, Naoko noticed something.</i>

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:02.750
<i>When she sprays water</i>
<i>over Gunpei's body…</i>

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:09.510
<i>somehow his skin briefly goes back</i>
<i>to the state it was in when he was alive.</i>

00:16:11.090 --> 00:16:13.130
He's so cute when he's asleep.

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:17.260
Gunpei, you are mine alone.

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:22.520
I'm the only one
who can take care of you, forever.

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:25.560
<i>What is this man?</i>

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:30.110
<i>He's definitely been dead the whole time.</i>

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:34.700
<i>I found out about Gunpei Kamafusa</i>

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:39.790
<i>when I visited this area several times</i>
<i>for the research of the specter legend</i>…

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:42.200
<i>which had been rumored since long ago.</i>

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:48.920
So you see, Mr. Kishibe,
this is definitely and absolutely…

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:51.380
a profitable deal for you!

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:52.300
Enough already!

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:55.550
I won't sell you my mountains, never!

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:58.510
Come now, Mr. Kishibe, just think.

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:06.440
Hello, this is Batsudera.

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:07.810
<i>I found out about this…</i>

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:12.440
<i>through a chance meeting with</i>
<i>Naoko Osato, and by reading her memory…</i>

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:15.990
<i>using my ability, Heaven's Door.</i>

00:17:16.070 --> 00:17:17.530
<i>Thanks to that stroke of luck,</i>

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:21.040
<i>I learned about the existence</i>
<i>of this man.</i>

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:22.490
Yes.

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:24.160
Hello.

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:27.040
Bad signal. Just wait a second, please.

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:30.460
What is he, this Gunpei?

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:34.170
I must find out what he is.

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:38.050
I want to know what he's after!

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:43.180
He's in the attic
above the closet in that house.

00:17:43.810 --> 00:17:46.810
You are Rohan Kishibe, aren't you?
You draw manga.

00:17:46.890 --> 00:17:47.730
What…

00:17:48.310 --> 00:17:51.940
I know. You've been snooping around here.

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:54.900
Who are you?

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:57.950
I've been told not to talk to strangers.

00:17:58.030 --> 00:17:58.860
You…

00:17:59.530 --> 00:18:03.700
There are lots
of perverts around nowadays.

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:07.540
Hey, wait!

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:16.760
Are you all right?

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:20.140
What are you doing running off like that--

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:23.890
Sh-- she's dead.

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:26.680
Wh-- what's happened?

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:28.690
Could it be…?

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:32.650
This is ridiculous.

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:34.690
This looks as if…

00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:37.780
as if I have done…

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:40.820
something to her here!

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:44.620
What the…? Is this girl…?

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:47.700
No way! It's impossible!

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:51.290
<i>Is she Gunpei's child?</i>

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:54.500
Naoko Osato, did she…

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:58.050
get pregnant by that body in the attic
and bear his child?!

00:18:58.130 --> 00:19:01.340
Mr. Kishibe, where are you?

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:05.890
Where in the world are you, Mr. Kishibe?

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:12.940
My God! It's going to possess me!

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:15.480
Heaven's Door!

00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:23.950
Damn it! The memories
of her life are fading away!

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:28.080
They'll all disappear! If they do,
she'll never come back to life again!

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:29.410
Before that…

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:34.330
I don't know Rohan Kishibe. Even if
I meet him, I won't be able to see him.

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:07.620
Mommy!

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:10.290
I'm hungry!

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:13.120
That was a close shave.

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:16.880
One second too late
and she would have possessed me.

00:20:18.420 --> 00:20:19.250
Or…

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:21.920
possibly ruined me!

00:20:22.420 --> 00:20:25.390
She was really formidable.
Such a close call.

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:30.470
Oh, here you are, Mr. Kishibe!
Sorry to leave you like that.

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:33.770
It was a call from my office.

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:36.310
I'll never, ever sell them to you.

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:39.360
What on earth?!

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:43.360
<i>This is the specter I went looking for.</i>

00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:46.410
<i>I'll call it</i>
<i>the "Mutsu-kabe Hill Specter."</i>

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:50.740
<i>I don't know how long it's been around.</i>
<i>Maybe a long time.</i>

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:53.870
<i>It's been feeding on human love</i>
<i>and the weakness of the human mind.</i>

00:20:54.460 --> 00:20:56.750
<i>It has humans do everything for it.</i>

00:20:56.830 --> 00:21:01.130
<i>It doesn't work, takes no responsibility</i>
<i>and suffers no hardship.</i>

00:21:02.590 --> 00:21:05.760
<i>Its only purpose is to reproduce.</i>

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:10.180
<i>Perhaps I could call it a creature.</i>

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:14.310
<i>The best moment of this creature's life is</i>

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:16.520
<i>when it dies in front of someone.</i>

00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:21.150
Maybe more of them
exist somewhere on Earth.

00:21:21.650 --> 00:21:25.610
It seems likely they continue to exist
by dying in front of someone.

00:21:26.150 --> 00:21:30.030
Is this a true story? That's unbelievable.

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:34.830
But it's not a complete lie.
You know anything about it?

00:21:34.910 --> 00:21:39.460
Yes, I remember there were
similar creatures in the Orion Nebula.

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:42.750
Hey, you can't just
barge into our meeting like--

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:48.050
I've always wanted to ask,
are you really an alien?

00:21:48.140 --> 00:21:53.390
Yes! I came from
the Magellanic Clouds to live here.

00:21:53.470 --> 00:21:56.440
But my spaceship is still waiting,
1.5 million kilometers up…

00:21:56.520 --> 00:21:58.900
This alien guy is such a bore.

00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:06.530
<i>How many Mutsu-kabe Hill Specters</i>
<i>are there? I'm not interested in that.</i>

00:22:07.900 --> 00:22:12.830
<i>Naoko Osato looks happy enough,</i>
<i>and I've found out the specter's purpose.</i>

00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:18.580
I'm no scholar or journalist.

00:22:20.130 --> 00:22:22.130
I'm just a manga artist.

00:22:23.130 --> 00:22:24.460
<i>Mommy!</i>

00:22:25.630 --> 00:22:29.840
<i>Will I marry a handsome man one day?</i>

00:22:31.010 --> 00:22:32.600
<i>Of course you will.</i>

00:24:08.480 --> 00:24:10.490
Subtitle translation by Songju Chong
